Is the model being fit in JAGS?  Maybe I(-10, 10) should be replaced by T(-10, 10)?  My other quick thought was that maybe "logit(mueps[i])<-mueps.prob[i]" would be better as mueps[i]<-logit(mueps.prob[i])?  For example, the logit of epsilon is defined as the combination of mueps and leps, which to me suggests that these terms should be logit transformations of the probabilities rather inverse logits of the probabilities.  "logit(mueps[i])<-mueps.prob[i]" constrains mueps to fall between 0.5 and 0.73.

